"REST API endpoints for workflow jobs - GitHub Docs (https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-jobs)\nciteturn1view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-jobs#re-run-a-job\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 315\nL0:   1.   2. 【0†GitHub Docs】\nL1: \nL2: Search or ask Copilot/\nL3: \nL4: Menu\nL5: \nL6: Collapse sidebar\nL7: \nL8: Expand sidebar\nL9: \nL10:   1. 【0†Home】\nL11:   2. 【1†REST API】\nL12:   3. 【2†Actions】\nL13:   4. Workflow jobs\nL14: \nL15: In this article\nL16: \nL17: # REST API endpoints for workflow jobs\nL18: \nL19: Use the REST API to interact with workflow jobs in GitHub Actions.\nL20: ## 【3†About workflow jobs in GitHub Actions】\nL21: \nL22: You can use the REST API to view logs and workflow jobs in GitHub Actions. A workflow job is a set of steps that execute on the same runner. For more information, see 【4†Workflow syntax for GitHub Actions】.\nL23: ## 【5†Get a job for a workflow run】\nL24: \nL25: Gets a specific job in a workflow run.\nL26: \nL27: Anyone with read access to the repository can use this endpoint.\nL28: \nL29: If the repository is private, OAuth tokens and personal access tokens (classic) need the `repo` scope to use this endpoint.\nL30: ### 【6†Fine-grained access tokens for \"Get a job for a workflow run\"】\nL31: \nL32: This endpoint works with the following fine-grained token types:\nL33: \nL34:   * 【7†GitHub App user access tokens】\nL35:   * 【8†GitHub App installation access tokens】\nL36:   * 【9†Fine-grained personal access tokens】\nL37: \nL38: The fine-grained token must have the following permission set:\nL39: \nL40:   * \"Actions\" repository permissions (read)\nL41: \nL42: This endpoint can be used without authentication or the aforementioned permissions if only public resources are requested.\nL43: ### 【10†Parameters for \"Get a job for a workflow run\"】\nL44: \nL45: Headers\nL46: `accept` string Setting to `application/vnd.github+json` is recommended.\nL47: Path parameters\nL48: `owner` string Required The account owner of the repository. The name is not case sensitive.\nL49: `repo` string Required The name of the repository without the `.git` extension. The name is not case sensitive.\nL50: `job_id` integer Required The unique identifier of the job.\nL51: ### 【11†HTTP response status codes for \"Get a job for a workflow run\"】\nL52: \nL53: Status code  | Description\nL54: --- | ---\nL55: `200`  | OK\nL56: \nL57: ### 【12†Code samples for \"Get a job for a workflow run\"】\nL58: #### Request example\nL59: \nL60: get/repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/jobs/{job_id}\nL61: \nL62:   * cURL\nL63: \nL64:   * JavaScript\nL65: \nL66:   * GitHub CLI\nL67: \nL68: Copy to clipboard curl request example\nL69: \nL70: `curl -L \\ -H \"Accept: application/vnd.github+json\" \\ -H \"Authorization: Bearer <YOUR-TOKEN>\" \\ -H \"X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10\" \\ https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/jobs/JOB_ID`\nL71: ####\nL72: \nL73: Response\nL74: \nL75:   * Example response\nL76: \nL77:   * Response schema\nL78: \nL79: `Status: 200`\nL80: `{ \"id\": 399444496, \"run_id\": 29679449, \"run_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/octo-org/octo-repo/actions/runs/29679449\", \"node_id\": \"MDEyOldvcmtmbG93IEpvYjM5OTQ0NDQ5Ng==\", \"head_sha\": \"f83a356604ae3c5d03e1b46ef4d1ca77d64a90b0\", \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/octo-org/octo-repo/actions/jobs/399444496\", \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/octo-org/octo-repo/runs/29679449/jobs/399444496\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T17:42:40Z\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T17:44:39Z\", \"name\": \"build\", \"steps\": [ { \"name\": \"Set up job\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 1, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:40.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:41.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Run actions/checkout@v2\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 2, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:41.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:45.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Set up Ruby\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 3, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:45.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:45.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Run actions/cache@v3\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 4, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:45.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:48.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Install Bundler\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 5, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:48.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:52.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Install Gems\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 6, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:52.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:53.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Run Tests\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 7, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:53.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:59.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Deploy to Heroku\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 8, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:42:59.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:44:39.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Post actions/cache@v3\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 16, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:44:39.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:44:39.000-08:00\" }, { \"name\": \"Complete job\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"conclusion\": \"success\", \"number\": 17, \"started_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:44:39.000-08:00\", \"completed_at\": \"2020-01-20T09:44:39.000-08:00\" } ], \"check_run_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/octo-org/octo-repo/check-runs/399444496\", \"labels\": [ \"self-hosted\", \"foo\", \"bar\" ], \"runner_id\": 1, \"runner_name\": \"my runner\", \"runner_group_id\": 2, \"runner_group_name\": \"my runner group\", \"workflow_name\": \"CI\", \"head_branch\": \"main\" }`\nL81: ## 【13†Download job logs for a workflow run】\nL82: \nL83: Gets a redirect URL to download a plain text file of logs for a workflow job. This link expires after 1 minute. Look for `Location:` in the response header to find the URL for the download.\nL84: \nL85: Anyone with read access to the repository can use this endpoint.\nL86: \nL87: If the repository is private, OAuth tokens and personal access tokens (classic) need the `repo` scope to use this endpoint.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRe-running workflows and jobs - GitHub Docs (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/manage-workflow-runs/re-run-workflows-and-jobs)\nciteturn1view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/manage-workflow-runs/re-run-workflows-and-jobs\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 167\nL0:   1.   2. 【0†GitHub Docs】\nL1: \nL2: Search or ask Copilot/\nL3: \nL4: Menu\nL5: \nL6: Collapse sidebar\nL7: \nL8: Expand sidebar\nL9: \nL10:   1. 【0†Home】\nL11:   2. 【1†GitHub Actions】\nL12:   3. 【2†How-tos】\nL13:   4. 【3†Manage workflow runs】\nL14:   5. Re-run workflows and jobs\nL15: \nL16: In this article\nL17: \nL18: # Re-running workflows and jobs\nL19: \nL20: You can re-run a workflow run, all failed jobs in a workflow run, or specific jobs in a workflow run up to 30 days after its initial run.\nL21: \nL22: Copy markdown\nL23: ## Who can use this feature?\nL24: \nL25: People with write permissions to a repository can re-run workflows in the repository.\nL26: \nL27: ## Tool navigation\nL28: \nL29:   * 【4†GitHub CLI】\nL30:   * 【5†Web browser】\nL31: ## In this article\nL32: \nL33:   * 【6†Re-running all the jobs in a workflow】\nL34: \nL35:   * 【7†Re-running failed jobs in a workflow】\nL36: \nL37:   * 【8†Re-running a specific job in a workflow】\nL38: \nL39:   * 【9†Reviewing previous workflow runs】\nL40: \nL41: Re-runs use the privileges of the actor who initially triggered the workflow, not the privileges of the actor who initiated the re-run. The workflow will also use the same `GITHUB_SHA` (commit SHA) and `GITHUB_REF` (git ref) of the original event that triggered the workflow run.\nL42: A workflow run can be re-run a maximum of 50 times. This limit includes both full re-runs and re-runs of a subset of jobs.\nL43: \nL44: When you re-run failed jobs or a specific job, GitHub also re-runs the jobs that depend on them. Jobs that aren't included keep their outputs from the previous attempt, which the newly run jobs can use.\nL45: \nL46: You can't re-run a workflow run, or any of its jobs, while the workflow is disabled. You need to enable the workflow first. See 【10†Disabling and enabling a workflow】.\nL47: ## 【6†Re-running all the jobs in a workflow】\nL48: \nL49:   1. On GitHub, navigate to the main page of the repository.\nL50: \nL51:   2. Under your repository name, click Actions.\nL52: \nL53: 【11†Image: Screenshot of the tabs for the \"github/docs\" repository. The \"Actions\" tab is highlighted with an orange outline.】\nL54: \nL55:   3. In the left sidebar, click the workflow you want to see.\nL56: \nL57: 【12†Image: Screenshot of the left sidebar of the \"Actions\" tab. A workflow, \"CodeQL,\" is outlined in dark orange.】\nL58:   4. From the list of workflow runs, click the name of the run to see the workflow run summary.\nL59: \nL60:   5. In the upper-right corner of the workflow, re-run jobs.\nL61: \nL62:      * If any jobs failed, select the Re-run jobs dropdown menu and click Re-run all jobs.\nL63:      * If no jobs failed, click Re-run all jobs.\nL64:   6. Optionally, to enable runner diagnostic logging and step debug logging for the re-run, select Enable debug logging. For more information, see 【13†Enabling debug logging】.\nL65: \nL66:   7. Click Re-run jobs.\nL67:   1. To re-run a failed workflow run, use the `run rerun` subcommand, replacing `RUN_ID` with the ID of the failed run that you want to re-run. If you don't specify a `run-id`, GitHub CLI returns an interactive menu for you to choose a recent failed run.\nL68: \nL69: Shell\nL70: \nL71:     gh run rerun RUN_ID\nL72: \nL73: \nL74:     `gh run rerun RUN_ID\nL75:     `\nL76: \nL77: To enable runner diagnostic logging and step debug logging for the re-run, use the `--debug` flag.\nL78: Shell\nL79: \nL80:     gh run rerun RUN_ID --debug\nL81: \nL82: \nL83:     `gh run rerun RUN_ID --debug\nL84:     `\nL85: \nL86:   2. To view the progress of the workflow run, use the `run watch` subcommand and select the run from the interactive list.\nL87: \nL88: Shell\nL89: \nL90:     gh run watch\nL91: \nL92: \nL93:     `gh run watch\nL94:     `\nL95: ## 【7†Re-running failed jobs in a workflow】\nL96: \nL97:   1. On GitHub, navigate to the main page of the repository.\nL98: \nL99:   2. Under your repository name, click Actions.\nL100: \nL101: 【11†Image: Screenshot of the tabs for the \"github/docs\" repository. The \"Actions\" tab is highlighted with an orange outline.】\nL102: \nL103:   3. In the left sidebar, click the workflow you want to see.\nL104: \nL105: 【12†Image: Screenshot of the left sidebar of the \"Actions\" tab. A workflow, \"CodeQL,\" is outlined in dark orange.】\nL106:   4. From the list of workflow runs, click the name of the run to see the workflow run summary.\nL107: \nL108:   5. In the upper-right corner of the workflow, select the Re-run jobs dropdown menu, and click Re-run failed jobs.\nL109: \nL110:   6. Optionally, to enable runner diagnostic logging and step debug logging for the re-run, select Enable debug logging. For more information, see 【13†Enabling debug logging】.\nL111: \nL112:   7. Click Re-run jobs.\nL113: To re-run failed jobs in a workflow run, use the `run rerun` subcommand with the `--failed` flag. Replace `RUN_ID` with the ID of the run for which you want to re-run failed jobs. If you don't specify a `run-id`, GitHub CLI returns an interactive menu for you to choose a recent failed run.\nL114: \nL115:     `gh run rerun RUN_ID --failed\nL116:     `\nL117: \nL118: To enable runner diagnostic logging and step debug logging for the re-run, use the `--debug` flag.\nL119: \nL120:     `gh run rerun RUN_ID --failed --debug\nL121:     `\nL122: ## 【8†Re-running a specific job in a workflow】\nL123: \nL124:   1. On GitHub, navigate to the main page of the repository.\nL125: \nL126:   2. Under your repository name, click Actions.\nL127: \nL128: 【11†Image: Screenshot of the tabs for the \"github/docs\" repository. The \"Actions\" tab is highlighted with an orange outline.】\nL129: \nL130:   3. In the left sidebar, click the workflow you want to see.\nL131: \nL132: 【12†Image: Screenshot of the left sidebar of the \"Actions\" tab. A workflow, \"CodeQL,\" is outlined in dark orange.】\nL133:   4. From the list of workflow runs, click the name of the run to see the workflow run summary.\nL134: \nL135:   5. Under the \"Jobs\" section of the left sidebar, next to the job that you want to re-run, click .\nL136: \n"
